The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
hlist_for_each_entry(daemon, &ecryptfs_daemon_hash[i], euid_chain) {
    rc = ecryptfs_exorcise_daemon(daemon);
}
```
Reason:
The use of `hlist_for_each_entry()` to iterate over the linked list while freeing elements can lead to a use-after-free condition. When an element is freed, the iterator may still reference that memory, causing undefined behavior.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
hlist_for_each_entry_safe(daemon, n, &ecryptfs_daemon_hash[i], euid_chain) {
    rc = ecryptfs_exorcise_daemon(daemon);
}
```
Reason:
The use of `hlist_for_each_entry_safe()` allows safe iteration over the list while freeing elements. It ensures that the iterator does not access freed memory by maintaining a separate pointer (`n`) to the next entry in the list, preventing use-after-free errors.

